 ## Aircraft inputs
 
-Above the table:
-
-- **Gallons per Hour** — defaults to `8`; persisted to `localStorage['navaid.aircraft']`.
-- **Taxi and Takeoff (gal)** — startup + taxi + takeoff allowance; defaults to `1.1`. Only added to the total when the origin waypoint matches an entry in `airfields.json` (by name OR by coordinates within ~100 m).
-- The same two figures are in **Settings** (*Gallons per hour*, *Taxi and takeoff (gal)*): one
-  profile, so a change in either place shows in the other at once.
+Above the table, the **Aircraft** row:
+
+- **The aircraft** — a listed type (C152, C172, PA28, DA40, SR22, AT3, C42, EV97, ULAC; **C172** by
+  default), or one of **your own aircraft**. Choosing a type fills every figure from its typical
+  manual values.
+- **Your own aircraft** — **New aircraft…** asks for its **call sign**: the code the
+  [flight plan form](Submit-Flight-Plan) files after `4X-` (e.g. `CRW`). It is listed as
+  `4X-CRW (C172)`; the same call sign twice is the same aircraft. Its **type** is then selected for
+  it in **Custom figures** (a listed type brings its figures; **Other…** takes any ICAO code), and
+  every figure changed while it is in use is saved into it.
+- **Custom figures** — a popover over the plan, like **Columns** and the departure time, so opening
+  it never makes the plan taller: call sign and type (your own aircraft only; dimmed, saying why,
+  for a listed type), usable fuel, climb speed, **descent rate**, **Restore C172 figures** and
+  **Delete** (asked in the app). Its ✕, Escape (the popover, not the plan) or a tap outside closes it.
+- **Gal/h** and **Taxi + T/O (gal)** — the aircraft's fuel figures. Taxi is added only when the
+  origin waypoint is an airfield in `airfields.json` (by name or within ~100 m). A figure changed
+  from the type's carries a dot, and its tooltip gives the type's value.
 - **V/S (ft/min)** above the vertical profile — shapes the **departure climb** on the profile and
   the **TOC** marker on the map; it does **not** change leg times or fuel (those are distance and
-  speed only), and a line under it says so. Also in Settings, the same value.
+  speed only), and a line under it says so.
 - **VOR** — optional reference VOR for Radial/DME columns. It syncs with the toolbar's **VOR ref** selector and persists to `navaid.vorRef`.
 
+The descent rate is what the [nav log](Print-and-Export) plans the descent with, unless a rate is
+set in the nav log itself (500 fpm for every listed type).
+
+Stored as `navaid.aircraft` (the aircraft in use) and `navaid.aircraftProfiles` (your own aircraft);
+both sync with Drive when **Sync settings too** is on.
+
 ## Radial / DME
 
 When a global VOR reference or a per-leg VOR override is selected, the table shows **Radial** and **DME** columns.
